00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:49.640
and be like, "Oh, I
guess it's not working."

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:52.830
We do not just check
for a bunch of diseases.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:56.580
When you come in for a checkup,
part of that is figuring out

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:58.450
what diseases we can actually screen for.

00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:00.020
There are some, like cancers.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:01.460
What diseases we can prevent.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:04.160
We could also look at what risks you face.

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:07.180
So get this, a patient comes
in, doesn't have liver disease,

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:09.560
but they talk to me honestly,
we have a good conversation

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:10.880
and finds out they're drinking

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:12.750
a bottle and a half of vodka a day.

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:14.630
It's a lot, but some people do do this.

00:06:14.630 --> 00:06:16.510
We have a conversation about, A,

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:18.950
what can we do to prevent them
from drinking and driving?

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:22.390
What we can do for them,
preventing themselves causing harm

00:06:22.390 --> 00:06:24.460
in other ways to themselves,
when they are inebriated.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:25.370
How can we get them

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:27.390
to cut down the amount
that they're drinking

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:28.920
so they can stay healthier longer.

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:31.380
Look at how much I've
affected their lifespan,

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:32.740
the progression of disease,

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:34.840
simply by having a good conversation.

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:36.550
That's what you should
expect from a doctor

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:37.760
when you go in for a physical.

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:39.340
And if you get anything less than that,

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:40.830
please look for a second opinion.

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:42.740
- Mr. Burns, I'm afraid you are

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:44.740
